{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"agent_message","text":"The level-5 trace exposes a suspicious alignment loop: the loaded vertical carrier moves down three cells, then up four, then down one—ending on its starting row—while horizontal carriers wrap a new peg into place. I’m testing whether the vertical detour is only collision avoidance or can be replaced by a different horizontal pre-alignment; eliminating it would save up to eight keys in one handoff."}}
